                <pb facs="0340" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">651.113/110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France (Edge) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-19T15:00:00+01:00">September 19, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 19—12:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>541. Your 327, September 17, 2 p.m. The French authorities have informed me
                    unofficially that France is now prepared to issue a decree reclassifying copper
                    as” a raw material just as soon as an agreement is reached between the two
                    Governments in regard to their present commercial treaty negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
